arguments.prompt:
You are implementing a Blazor Web App for a logistics company that tracks shipments. The project is already scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-350e6b1916df4b9e9175331f112a6a2b/ShipmentTracker/` using `dotnet new blazor -int Auto -ai -au Individual`.

## Project Structure
- **Server project**: `/tmp/sv-350e6b1916df4b9e9175331f112a6a2b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/`
- **Client project**: `/tmp/sv-350e6b1916df4b9e9175331f112a6a2b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/`
- Solution file: `/tmp/sv-350e6b1916df4b9e9175331f112a6a2b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.sln`

## Key Architecture Rules (Auto Global mode)
- Interactive components MUST go in the `.Client` project (`ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/`)
- Components cannot access DB directly — must use HTTP APIs
- Pattern: Define interface in `.Client`, implement with HttpClient in `.Client`, implement with EF Core in server, register both in respective `Program.cs`
- API endpoints go in server `Program.cs`
- Both `Program.cs` files must register matching services
- No `@rendermode` needed on pages (global mode sets it in App.razor)
- Identity/Account pages are static SSR — don't modify them

## Requirements
1. Dispatchers view a list of shipments with status and destination
2. Customers check their shipment status and estimated delivery
3. Every page has interactive controls
4. Individual accounts auth is already scaffolded

## What to Implement

### 1. Data Model (Server project)

Create `/tmp/sv-350e6b1916df4b9e9175331f112a6a2b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/Data/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Data;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime CreatedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime? EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public string? CustomerEmail { get; set; }
    public string? Notes { get; set; }
}

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Cancelled
}
```

### 2. Update ApplicationDbContext

Edit `/tmp/sv-350e6b1916df4b9e9175331f112a6a2b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs` to add `DbSet<Shipment>` and seed sample data:

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Identity.EntityFrameworkCore;
using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Data;

public class ApplicationDbContext(DbContextOptions<ApplicationDbContext> options) : IdentityDbContext<ApplicationUser>(options)
{
    public DbSet<Shipment> Shipments => Set<Shipment>();

    protected override void OnModelCreating(ModelBuilder builder)
    {
        base.OnModelCreating(builder);

        builder.Entity<Shipment>(entity =>
        {
            entity.HasIndex(s => s.TrackingNumber).IsUnique();
        });

        // Seed sample shipments
        builder.Entity<Shipment>().HasData(
            new Shipment { Id = 1, TrackingNumber = "TRK-10001", Origin = "New York, NY", Destination = "Los Angeles, CA", Status = ShipmentStatus.InTransit, CreatedDate = new DateTime(2026, 5, 28, 0, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc), EstimatedDelivery = new DateTime(2026, 6, 4, 0, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc), CustomerEmail = "alice@example.com", Notes = "Fragile — handle with care" },
            new Shipment { Id = 2, TrackingNumber = "TRK-10002", Origin = "Chicago, IL", Destination = "Houston, TX", Status = ShipmentStatus.Pending, CreatedDate = new DateTime(2026, 6, 1, 0, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc), EstimatedDelivery = new DateTime(2026, 6, 7, 0, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc), CustomerEmail = "bob@example.com" },
            new Shipment { Id = 3, TrackingNumber = "TRK-10003", Origin = "Seattle, WA", Destination = "Miami, FL", Status = ShipmentStatus.Delivered, CreatedDate = new DateTime(2026, 5, 20, 0, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc), EstimatedDelivery = new DateTime(2026, 5, 27, 0, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc), CustomerEmail = "carol@example.com" },
            new Shipment { Id = 4, TrackingNumber = "TRK-10004", Origin = "Denver, CO", Destination = "Phoenix, AZ", Status = ShipmentStatus.OutForDelivery, CreatedDate = new DateTime(2026, 5, 30, 0, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc), EstimatedDelivery = new DateTime(2026, 6, 2, 0, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc), CustomerEmail = "dave@example.com" },
            new Shipment { Id = 5, TrackingNumber = "TRK-10005", Origin = "Boston, MA", Destination = "Atlanta, GA", Status = ShipmentStatus.PickedUp, CreatedDate = new DateTime(2026, 6, 1, 0, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc), EstimatedDelivery = new DateTime(2026, 6, 6, 0, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc), CustomerEmail = "eve@example.com" }
        );
    }
}
```

### 3. Create a migration and update the DB

Run:
```
cd /tmp/sv-350e6b1916df4b9e9175331f112a6a2b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker
dotnet ef migrations add AddShipments
dotnet ef database update
```

If `dotnet ef` is not available, install it: `dotnet tool install --global dotnet-ef`

### 4. Shared DTO (Client project)

Create `/tmp/sv-350e6b1916df4b9e9175331f112a6a2b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/ShipmentDto.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client;

public class ShipmentDto
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Status { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public DateTime CreatedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime? EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public string? CustomerEmail { get; set; }
    public string? Notes { get; set; }
}
```

### 5. Service Interface (Client project)

Create `/tmp/sv-350e6b1916df4b9e9175331f112a6a2b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/IShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetAllShipmentsAsync();
    Task<ShipmentDto?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<ShipmentDto> CreateShipmentAsync(ShipmentDto shipment);
    Task<ShipmentDto> UpdateShipmentAsync(ShipmentDto shipment);
}
```

### 6. Client-side HttpClient implementation (Client project)

Create `/tmp/sv-350e6b1916df4b9e9175331f112a6a2b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/ShipmentHttpService.cs`:
```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client;

public class ShipmentHttpService(HttpClient http) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<ShipmentDto>>("api/shipments") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        var response = await http.GetAsync($"api/shipments/track/{Uri.EscapeDataString(trackingNumber)}");
        if (response.StatusCode == System.Net.HttpStatusCode.NotFound)
            return null;
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>();
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto> CreateShipmentAsync(ShipmentDto shipment)
    {
        var response = await http.PostAsJsonAsync("api/shipments", shipment);
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return (await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>())!;
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto> UpdateShipmentAsync(ShipmentDto shipment)
    {
        var response = await http.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{shipment.Id}", shipment);
