## Key Architecture Rules (Auto Global mode)
- Interactive components MUST go in the `.Client` project (`ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/`)
- Components cannot access DB directly — must use HTTP APIs
- Pattern: Define interface in `.Client`, implement with HttpClient in `.Client`, implement with EF Core in server, register both in respective `Program.cs`
- API endpoints go in server `Program.cs`
- Both `Program.cs` files must register matching services
- No `@rendermode` needed on pages (global mode sets it in App.razor)
- Identity/Account pages are static SSR — don't modify them

## Requirements
1. Dispatchers view a list of shipments with status and destination
2. Customers check their shipment status and estimated delivery
